From 88d72ac6af5891b449dc10858df576a92d666d68 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: exeroom536 <352890649+exeroom536@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 12:52:04 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 09/53] util: an mdmon that is a zombie is not running

mdmon_running() takes an mdmon for running while kill(pid, 0) finds it.
A zombie it still finds.  In the shutdown ramfs (systemd's exitrd,
dracut's shutdown) pid 1 does not reap, and an mdmon that left on
SIGTERM keeps its pid file (the mdmon taking over is to clean up, see
wait_and_act()): it is "running" for good.  mdadm --stop of its
container then waits the full 5 s for it to leave and says "mdmon for
... is still running"; mdmon_take_array() starts no new mdmon for a
member array, which stays readonly; wait_for_mdmon() takes the zombie
for the mdmon it waits for.

Tell a zombie from a running mdmon in mdmon_running(): move is_zombie()
from mdmon.c (try_kill_monitor() keeps using it) to util.c.

IMSM containers on loop devices, and AMD RAIDXpert2 ones (later in this
series), a RAID1 in each, in a pid namespace whose pid 1 does not reap;
mdmon ended with SIGTERM.  Without the change, mdadm -I of the container
leaves the RAID1 readonly with no mdmon, and mdadm --stop of the
container takes 5.05 s and says "still running"; with it a new mdmon
takes the RAID1 and --stop takes 24-36 ms.  With a pid 1 that reaps,
the same steps without the change: a new mdmon, --stop in 23 ms.

Written by Claude Opus 5.5, an AI model by Anthropic.
